 "passCount": 0,
 "reading": "A close at the top of the day does not tell gold's next three days anything an ordinary day does not. Out of sample the full-close buy made +0.057R before costs and −0.008R net a trade (n 238), below the same buy after every day of the same year (−0.047R excess, month t −0.76); it was +0.057R excess in 2007-16 (t 0.63), so the sign flips. The wide-day version (T2) and the sell after a close at the low (T3) are the same: no test is above its placebo median by enough (10, 14 and 15 of 40 beaten), and the sells lose net out of sample (−0.142R, t −2.21) as every gold short in this series has. What the buys earn is gold's drift of the year, which the baseline already holds. Not an edge, not a filter, no proposal."
}
